[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) was marked known: one issue, one fix queued. Its reports held two
problems with two different outcomes. #4471 closed on 5 October.

<Callout kind="warn">
Not one issue. Each problem below has its own ticket, now closed: <code>parser</code> fixed, <code>hint</code> won't fix.
</Callout>

## What the reports show

<ProblemTable
  ticket={4471}
  issues={{
    parser: 'https://github.com/navamara55/megadev-w1-c3-what-it-shows/issues/1',
    hint: 'https://github.com/navamara55/megadev-w1-c3-what-it-shows/issues/2',
  }}
/>

- **`parser`**: the shared parser reads every date month first. Our tenants write the day first,
  so day and month swap: 2 July becomes 7 February. This is what #4471 describes. A few of
  these reports describe the date as moved by a day; the desk noted them in `desk-notes.json`.
  By tenant and channel their cause is the parser, so they count here.
  **Fixed:** `fix(dates): parse dd/mm for eu locales`.
- **`hint`**: the `booking-v3` form prints `MM/DD/YYYY` under its date field and reads the date
  day first. People type what the hint says. Only form reports from `booking-v3` tenants.
  Fixing the parser does not fix the form. The #4471 table marks this cause "no ticket of its
  own"; it has one now. **Won't fix:** the `booking-v3` form is retired.

## Why one ticket

[Decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject) merges on the subject line alone. Every
subject here says "wrong day" in some form, so every report landed in #4471. The cause depends
on the tenant, its booking form and the channel the report came through, and the subject says
none of that. Intake's tag guesses from the reporter's browser, so it does not settle it either.

## How the count works

One id, one report: the ticket export repeats some rows. Each report goes to one problem, its
cause from `causes.ts`: the tenant's locale, its booking form, and the channel.
The table is built from the export at render time.

